Zcash gets a JavaScript toolkit for app makers

@ZcashLabs has released Zcash JS, a free, open-source developer kit for building $ZEC apps in JavaScript and TypeScript. It lets developers read chain data, run lightweight wallets, and sign and send transactions from web browsers and Node servers.

The release is an early, experimental test version, and a full send-and-receive run in a live browser has not been signed off yet. Zcash Labs says it will keep maintaining the kit and grow more tools around it. The main @Zcash account shared the launch and called on developers to take notice.

