AI is eating the world’s hard drives, and Filecoin wants in

@Seagate, the world’s largest hard drive maker, says most of its high-capacity data-center drive output is already allocated through 2028, and Western Digital is also sold out for this year. Prices have followed suit, with data-center memory and storage drives costing more than twice as much as a year earlier, according to research firm Dell’Oro.

@Filecoin, the storage network behind filecoin:native, is pitching its spare room as the answer. The network offers online storage capacity today, rented by independent providers, so it doesn’t depend on new drive orders to grow.

